Article 1 (Enforcement date)
This Act shall enter into force on September 21, 2018; provided, the amended provisions of Article 35 (2) (only applicable to calculating the amount of pension benefits for a survivor of a teacher or staff who died while performing official duties) and Article 42 (1) that applies mutatis mutandis Articles 36 (2) and 37 (2) of the Public Officials' Accident Compensation Act shall enter into force on March 20, 2018.
Article 2 (Applicability to basis for calculating amount of benefits)
(1) Amended Article 35 (2) that provides for the basic amount of minimum compensation shall also apply to a person who died before the date of enforcement specified in Article 1 of the Addenda and grounds for paying a pension benefit for the survivor of a teacher or staff who died while performing official duties have arisen (such person includes anyone who is receiving a survivors’ pension under Article 56 (1) 3 of the former Public Officials Pension Act (that was in force before it was wholly amended by Act No. 15523; hereinafter the same applies) which is applicable mutatis mutandis under the former Article 42 (1) before the enforcement of this Act).
(2) The amount of benefits payable under paragraph (1) shall apply, beginning with the payment date of benefits that first arrives after the date of enforcement specified in the proviso of Article 1 of the Addenda.
Article 3 (Applicability to pension payments for survivor of teacher or staff who died while performing official duties)
(1) Article 36 (2) of the Public Officials' Accident Compensation Act which is applicable mutatis mutandis under the amended provisions of Article 42 (1) shall also apply to a person regarding whom grounds for paying a pension benefit for the survivor of a teacher or staff who died while performing official duties arose before the date of enforcement specified in the proviso of Article 1 of the Addenda (such person includes anyone who is receiving a survivors’ pension under Article 56 (1) 3 of the former Public Officials Pension Act).
(2) The amount of benefits payable under paragraph (1) shall apply, beginning with the payment date of benefits that first arrives after the date of enforcement specified in the proviso of Article 1 of the Addenda.
Article 4 (Applicability to adjustment of benefits under other statutes)
`Article 41 (3) through (6) of the Public Officials Pension Act which is applicable mutatis mutandis under the amended provisions of Article 42 (1) shall apply, beginning with a person regarding whom grounds for paying a benefit arise after this Act enters into force.
Article 5 (Applicability to payment of and prior claim for split pension)
(1) Articles 45 through 48 of the Public Officials Pension Act (except for the criteria for recognition of the marriage period under Article 45 (1) and (4) of the Public Officials Pension Act) which is applicable mutatis mutandis under the amended provisions of Article 42 (1) shall apply, beginning with a person who divorced on or after January 1, 2016. In this case, the marriage period during which a split pension is payable includes the marriage period during which a current or former spouse worked as a teacher or staff before January 1, 2016.
(2) A person who satisfies the requirements under Article 45 (1) 1 and 2 of the Public Officials Pension Act which is applicable mutatis mutandis under the amended provisions of Article 42 (1) may receive a split pension, notwithstanding Article 45 (1) 3 of the same Act, if the person reaches the age in the years specified in the following:
1. From 2016 to 2021: 60 years of age;
2. From 2022 to 2023: 61 years of age;
3. From 2024 to 2026: 62 years of age;
4. From 2027 to 2029: 63 years of age;
5. From 2030 to 2032: 64 years of age.
(3) Article 49 of the Public Officials Pension Act which is applicable mutatis mutandis under the amended provisions of Article 42 (1) shall also apply to a person who divorced during the period from January 1, 2016 to the date of enforcement of this Act if the person files a prior claim for split payment of the lump-sum retirement pension, lump-sum retirement pension after deductions, or lump-sum payment on retirement after this Act enters into force. In this case, the marriage period during which the lump-sum retirement pension, lump-sum retirement pension after deductions, or lump-sum payment on retirement can be split includes the marriage period during which a current or former spouse worked as a teacher or staff before this Act enters into force.
Article 6 (Applicability to change of definition of marriage period)
The marriage period provided in Article 45 (1) and (4) of the Public Officials Pension Act which is applicable mutatis mutandis under the amended provisions of Article 42 (1) shall apply, beginning with the first case in which grounds for paying a split pension arise after this Act enters into force.
Article 7 (Special cases concerning payment of benefits and interest after grounds for limiting benefits cease to exist)
Article 65 (2) of the Public Officials Pension Act which is applicable mutatis mutandis under the amended provisions of Article 42 (1) shall also apply to a person regarding whom grounds for limiting benefits ceased to exist retroactively before this Act enters into force. In this case, notwithstanding Article 54, no claim for payment of the amount specified in Article 65 (2) of the Public Officials Pension Act can be filed upon the expiration of the five-year period following the date of enforcement of this Act.
Article 8 (Applicability to payment of rehabilitation benefits)
(1) Articles 26 and 27 of the Public Officials' Accident Compensation Act which is applicable mutatis mutandis under the amended provisions of Article 42 (1) shall also apply to a person regarding whom a decision to take medical care related to the performance of official duties was made under Article 35 of the former Public Officials Pension Act which is applicable mutatis mutandis under former Article 42 (1) before this Act enters into force.
(2) The amount of benefits payable under paragraph (1) shall apply, beginning with a person who does rehabilitation exercise or takes counseling after this Act enters into force.
Article 9 Omitted.

